    "scope": "1141 Git-tracked evidence paths, 301 members inside tar.gz, gzip contents and early baseline-index. Case/punctuation/accents normalized. Paper titles used for replication releases."
  },
  "methods": [
    "Joined 42 MATLAB v7.3 signals through their own dSPACE Y/XIndex on the ~1 kHz command clock, including the corresponding ~4 kHz inverter and independent table traces. The largest nearest-neighbor discrepancy is zero in the released files. RMS and ranges refer to the joined grid, not 4 kHz peaks. The README identifies a 400 kg table, 0.72 m travel and deactivated position controller. Seven tuning methods are named across the release.",
    "Computed velocity error from v_ref minus measured motor/table velocity, and request-versus-inverter torque RMS from u_motor [rot] and M_KGT_act. Counted each 1→0 sigEnable edge, same-row lastError and subsequent disabled interval, and measured resulting displacement. Force minima/maxima counts cover the full file."
  ],
  "results": [
    "All 42 runs give 584,060 synchronized command/inverter/table records; 12 ForceSweep, 14 VelSweep, 6 VelocityRamp, 10 extra H-infinity sweeps. Thirty-two release F_nut_sum; the ten extra H-infinity sweeps omit this channel.",
    "At 0.247996682 s in VelocityRamp/SymmetricOpt.mat (row 248, zero based), sigEnable falls and lastError changes from 0 to 2. Across the remaining 1,001 samples, requested torque is exactly −94.78474 Nm while inverter torque changes from −55.04761 to −0.01831 Nm; table position spans 38.2267 mm. This is the only disable event and the only experiment with nonzero error.",
    "The same full file hits F_nut_sum extrema −3999.999997 N (16 samples) and +3999.877927 N (7). Its 152.00 mm/s full-run table speed error includes disabled control; the five other recorded ramp traces range from 2.297 to 4.757 mm/s."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The source defines code 2 only as an error code and gives no cause in this release. A frozen request after disabling cannot establish actuator clipping. Repeated force-channel extrema suggest measurement range effects, with no certified saturation bit.",
    "Whole-run errors include rest periods and shutdown transients. The six ramp captures have different sample counts and capture starts. The missing DisturbanceOpt ramp and missing nut-force channels in ten sweeps limit balanced comparisons. Motor torque is an inverter-side signal; the independent sensors are the table readout and nut-force measurement."
  ],
